## 7-Nov-9:18pm-PST/PDT — the naming settlement and the two shelves

cs_office is the settled public name — lowercase, with the
underscore, named for the Counter-Strike map. The
workstream's public page stands in this drawer, at
docs/infrastructure-documents/project/cs_office.md.

The two-shelf rule, in brief. The public shelf holds the
name, the method, the principles, and counts. The private
shelf holds identities, cases, unfixed findings, and crash
data.

Work under examination is referred to by label only —
Target A and Target B. Target A is the active case and
Target B is the learning ground. The mapping from a label
to what it labels sits on the private shelf.

Marking: hp0
